 [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/391"} "Meilahti, Helsinki"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/158147"} "32 from 16 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Switzerland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/39745"} "Hans Kalt"] ", one of the 1948 silver medalists, returned to the Olympics in 1952 with a new partner, " [:a {:href "/athletes/39797"} "Kurt Schmid"] ", in an attempt to capture the crown that had eluded him in the previous edition. Kalt and Schmid were the 1950 European Champions, but they faced serious competition from " [:a {:href "/athletes/35709"} "Michel Knuysen"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/35656"} "Bob Baetens"] " of Belgium, the reigning European champions. Other contenders included " [:a {:href "/athletes/39930"} "Bernt Torberntsson"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/39882"} "Evert Gunnarsson"] ", the 1949 European Champions, and " [:a {:href "/athletes/36520"} "Bent Jensen"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/36617"} "Palle Tillisch"] " of Denmark, the 1951 European runners-up."] "\n\n" [:p {} "All of these nations survived the opening round but, by the end of the semi-final repêchage, Denmark and Sweden had been eliminated, leaving what many felt would be a race for podium spots between Switzerland, Belgium, and the strong British duo of " [:a {:href "/athletes/37247"} "David Callender"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/37278"} "Chris Davidge"] ". In the final, Switzerland led for short period, but were soon overtaken by Belgium, and then by a surprise push from the entirely unheralded United States team of " [:a {:href "/athletes/40756"} "Charlie Logg"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/40839"} "Tom Price"] ". Belgium nearly held the Americans off, but the latter pulled ahead in the final 100 meters and earned their gold medal with almost three seconds to spare ahead of the Belgians. Switzerland finished in a distant third, with Great Britain behind and France’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/37103"} "Jean-Pierre Souche"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/36982"} "René Guissart"] " completing the course nearly half a minute after the winners."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/40756"} "Charlie Logg"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/40839"} "Tom Price"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/35709"} "Michel Knuysen"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/35656"} "Bob Baetens"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BEL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/BEL.png"}] "BEL"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/39797"} "Kurt Schmid"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/39745"} "Hans Kalt"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SUI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SUI.png"}] "SUI"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/37247"} "David Callender"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/37278"} "Chris Davidge"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "5"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/37103"} "Jean-Pierre Souche"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/36982"} "René Guissart"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "pad